<title>NORWAY: Braathens buys six Boeing planes.</title>
<headline>Braathens buys six Boeing planes.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian airline Braathens SAFE ASA said on Monday it had ordered six planes of the next generation of Boeing 737 model for 1.5 billion crowns over three years.</p>
<p>The first plane is due for delivery in July or August 1998.</p>
<p>Braathens also has secure options for another 10 Boeing 737-700 aircraft for delivery after 2000, the company said in a statement to the Oslo bourse.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
